{
  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "The current best (config_036, scvi_n200 + ViT-L, avgpool, concat, 0.715 acc) shows that the RNA encoder is the dominant factor: switching from PCA to scvi_n200 gave a ~9-point gain, while avgpool vs. transformer aggregation previously showed a ~4-point gap (0.619 vs 0.579) but only under the much simpler PCA representation. config_038 isolates a single variable—changing aggregation from avgpool to transformer—while keeping the strong scvi_n200 + ViT-L backbone. This tests whether the learned, structured embeddings from scvi_n200 interact differently with attention-based aggregation than with simple pooling. If transformer matches or beats avgpool here, it reveals an important encoder-aggregation interaction and opens a new design axis; if it underperforms, it confirms avgpool is robustly superior regardless of encoder quality. This is the most informative single-variable extension of the current best, balancing exploitation of the scvi_n200+ViT-L direction with exploration of a design choice whose prior evidence was collected under a weaker RNA encoder."
}

